&lt;h2 id=&#34;details&#34;&gt;Details
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Most documentation is available on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://systemd.io/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;systemd&amp;rsquo;s web site&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assorted, older, general information about systemd can be found in the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Software/systemd&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;systemd Wiki&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Information about build requirements is provided in the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;README&#34; &gt;README file&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consult our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;NEWS&#34; &gt;NEWS file&lt;/a&gt; for information about what&amp;rsquo;s new in the most recent systemd versions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please see the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;docs/ARCHITECTURE.md&#34; &gt;Code Map&lt;/a&gt; for information about this repository&amp;rsquo;s layout and content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please see the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;docs/HACKING.md&#34; &gt;Hacking guide&lt;/a&gt; for information on how to hack on systemd and test your modifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please see our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;docs/CONTRIBUTING.md&#34; &gt;Contribution Guidelines&lt;/a&gt; for more information about filing GitHub Issues and posting GitHub Pull Requests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When preparing patches for systemd, please follow our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;docs/CODING_STYLE.md&#34; &gt;Coding Style Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are looking for support, please contact our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://lists.freedesktop.org/mailman/listinfo/systemd-devel&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;mailing list&lt;/a&gt;, join our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://web.libera.chat/#systemd&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;IRC channel #systemd on libera.chat&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://matrix.to/#/#systemd-project:matrix.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Matrix channel&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stable branches with backported patches are available in the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/systemd/systemd-stable&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;stable repo&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a security bug bounty program sponsored by the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.sovereigntechfund.de/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Sovereign Tech Fund&lt;/a&gt; hosted on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://yeswehack.com/programs/systemd-bug-bounty-program&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;YesWeHack&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Repositories with distribution packages built from git main are &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://software.opensuse.org//download.html?project=system%3Asystemd&amp;amp;package=systemd&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;available on OBS&lt;/a&gt;,
and also repositories with &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://software.opensuse.org//download.html?project=system%3Asystemd%3Astable&amp;amp;package=systemd&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;packages built from the latest stable release&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
